33,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
36,2,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
37,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are concerning. The late-turn pool has thinned significantly since the recruitment freeze, leaving us reliant on overtime for final departures and overnight works. We are operating with a dangerously fragile human foundation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,My records show that we've tried some of this before. The contactless ferry trial and the late-evening timetable pilot actually worked fine eight years ago. We don't need to be afraid of those ideas; they've already been proven.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The records confirm my suspicions. We face significant risks from unrecorded voids in pre-war shells, and a lack of agreement on passenger data between ferry and rail offices creates a hidden administrative barrier.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found some things that are a bit worrying. The ticketing fees are so high now that they're more than what we have for resurfacing, and the paving rates keep going up. It feels like the money is... disappearing.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Guess what! I found a big secret! Everyone complains about the crowds, but the counts show they clear just like they used to. The real mystery is that waiting for connections is what's actually making everyone late!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, your discovery about connections is interesting, but it adds pressure to a system already at its limit. If we change the timetable to fix connections, we risk further exhausting the thinned late-turn pool.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, we can't just be afraid of the staff being tired. If the late-evening pilot worked eight years ago, it means there's a way to do it right. We just need to stop guessing and use what actually worked!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, a pilot from eight years ago does not account for the current state of our infrastructure. The unrecorded voids in the pre-war shells are a physical reality that can stall any plan, regardless of past success.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think @Toshio is right about the risks. But I'm also worried that if we ignore the costs, like the rising paving rates, we'll just end up fighting over the budget again instead of helping the passengers.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, but if we don't fix the connections, people will just keep complaining! Maybe we can find a way to make it easier for the staff too? I want to find a solution that makes everyone smile!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, a solution that makes everyone smile is a lovely goal, but it requires a realistic workforce. My data shows roadway and signals crews are a third below establishment. We cannot simply add complexity without people to manage it.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're just focusing on the gaps! If we look at the accessibility records, some rebuilds finished right on time. We can't just give up because things are hard; we have to be brave and use the plans that actually work!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, bravery is not a substitute for a survey. The records show that work in pre-war shells has stopped for weeks due to unrecorded voids. No amount of courage can fill a physical hole in the ground.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that the physical risks are scary. But I'm also worried about the money. I found that the technology line was trimmed again, and we're paying so much to ticketing contractors... I'm afraid we'll commit to a plan we can't actually afford.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be sad! We can find a way! But @Toshio and @Victoria, if we only worry about holes and tired people, we'll never fix the connections! That's where the real time is disappearing!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Toshio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"It is not a matter of being afraid, @Sakura, but of being honest. If we prioritize connections without addressing the staffing deficit, we are merely shifting the burden onto a crew that is already breaking.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, being honest means admitting we've succeeded before! The accessibility rebuilds worked and the pilots worked. We just need to stop letting the current problems paralyze us and actually implement the things that are proven to work!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Proven success in the past is a comfort, but it is not a guarantee. We must prioritize a plan that avoids the pre-war shells and the ferry-rail data conflict, or we risk another systemic stall.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should be careful. If we pick a plan that needs a lot of new technology or roadworks, the trimmed budget and rising paving rates might make it impossible. I don't want us to start another argument over the money.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I'm not trying to be a troublemaker, but we can't just ignore the passengers! If we only fix the things that are easy, the people waiting for connections will still be grumpy. Let's find a plan that's a win-win for everyone!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
