61,3,,status,Sakura,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
62,3,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Looking at the options, Plan B is a direct threat to our stability. Extending night services would place an impossible burden on a late-turn pool that is already thinned to the breaking point.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're doing it again! The late-evening pilot from eight years ago proved we can handle this. We just need to use the right roster from back then instead of giving up!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, a roster from eight years ago is a ghost. It does not solve the current staffing deficit @Victoria identified, nor does it address the physical and administrative risks I have uncovered. Plan B is a gamble.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Plan D. Replacing the ticketing system sounds good, but I found that we're already paying so much to three different contractors. I'm afraid the transition costs will be huge.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I think Plan A is the most exciting! It's in the mid-city where I saw the timed runs taking longer, and it could really help people get across town faster without waiting for connections!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, Plan A is appealing, but rebuilt boarding islands and dedicated lanes require roadway and signals crews. With those teams a third below establishment, I worry we lack the hands to build it.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, we can't just stop every time we're short-staffed! The accessibility records show we've finished rebuilds on time before. We just need to be determined and push through to get it done!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Determination cannot override physical reality. Plan C is the most dangerous; reworking older stations means entering the pre-war shells where unrecorded voids have already stalled projects for weeks. It is a recipe for failure.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think @Toshio is right about the risks of Plan C. And @Victoria's point about the crews makes me worry about Plan A too. If paving rates keep rising, the cost of those lanes might... become a huge problem.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't let the money monsters scare you! If we fix the mid-city route, maybe more people will use it and we'll get more money! Plus, it's better than Plan D, which sounds like a big computer headache!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, the ""computer headache"" of Plan D is actually the most sustainable option for our staff. It avoids the physical construction risks @Toshio mentioned and the staffing deficits I found in the roadway crews.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you're just picking the easiest path! Plan D is exactly what we tried with the ferry link eight years ago, and it worked perfectly. We don't need to be scared of it; we just need to do it right this time!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the ferry link was a pilot, not a full integration. My findings show that the ferry and rail back offices still cannot agree on common passenger data terms. Plan D is an administrative minefield.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm really torn. @Victoria says Plan D is easier on the staff, but @Toshio is right about the data conflict. And with the technology line being trimmed, I'm scared we can't even afford the software.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, @Daisuke, if Plan D is a minefield and a headache, let's forget it! Plan A is the only one that actually fixes the mid-city slowness I found. We just have to be clever about how we build it!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, being clever cannot replace missing personnel. However, if we must choose, Plan A is more viable than B or C. It avoids the late-turn crisis and the pre-war voids. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, finally! I've been saying we need to be brave. Plan A is a real improvement, and we've proven we can handle rebuilds. I'm not letting us settle for nothing. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"Plan A is the only logical choice. It avoids the physical voids of Plan C, the administrative deadlock of Plan D, and the staffing collapse of Plan B. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm still a bit scared about the paving costs and the trimmed budget, but everyone else seems so sure. I don't want to cause an argument... I'll trust you all. I vote for Plan A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! I'm so happy we all agree! Plan A is the best because it fixes the mid-city slowness and helps people stop waiting forever for connections. Let's make the passengers smile! I vote for Plan A!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
